Feature: SQL Transformation Logic Enhancement for pat_account Table

  The transformation logic for the pat_account table must be updated to align with the latest source-to-target mapping specifications. This includes precise transformation rules for prescriber_id, prescriber_key, patient_sf_id, hash_key, and last_modified_date columns, with strict validation and error handling.

  Background:
    Given the source table "purgo_playground.p_account" contains columns:
      | patient_foundation_shipment | prescriber_name_c | prescriber_name_c_address | patinet_c | recordtypeid | id | accountid |
    And the target table "purgo_playground.pat_account" contains columns:
      | patient_foundation_shipment | prescriber_id | prescriber_key | patient_sf_id | service_request_type | case_sf_id | account_id | hash_key | last_modified_date |
    And the mapping specification is provided in "source_target_mapping_specifications.xlsx"
    And the error log table "purgo_playground.pat_account_error_log" is available for error scenarios

  # Happy Path Scenarios

  Scenario: Transform prescriber_id with uppercase and DR. prefix
    Given a source record with prescriber_name_c = "john smith"
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then prescriber_id in the target should be "DR.JOHN SMITH"

  Scenario: Transform prescriber_id when DR. prefix already present
    Given a source record with prescriber_name_c = "Dr.Jane Doe"
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then prescriber_id in the target should be "DR.JANE DOE"

  Scenario: Transform prescriber_key with DR. prefix if not present
    Given a source record with prescriber_name_c_address = "michael brown"
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then prescriber_key in the target should be "DR.MICHAEL BROWN"

  Scenario: Transform prescriber_key when DR. prefix already present
    Given a source record with prescriber_name_c_address = "Dr.Alice White"
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then prescriber_key in the target should be "DR.ALICE WHITE"

  Scenario Outline: Transform patient_sf_id based on patinet_c value
    Given a source record with patinet_c = <patinet_c>
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then patient_sf_id in the target should be <expected_patient_sf_id>

    Examples:
      | patinet_c   | expected_patient_sf_id |
      | "PAT12345"  | "PAT12345"            |
      | "12345PAT"  | "12345PAT"            |
      | "12345"     | NULL                  |
      | NULL        | NULL                  |

  Scenario Outline: Generate hash_key using underscore separator and correct columns
    Given a source record with patinet_c = <patinet_c>, recordtypeid = <recordtypeid>, id = <id>
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then hash_key in the target should be "<patinet_c>_<recordtypeid>_<id>"

    Examples:
      | patinet_c   | recordtypeid | id        |
      | "PAT12345"  | "RT01"       | "C001"    |
      | "PAT67890"  | "RT02"       | "C002"    |

  Scenario: Set last_modified_date to current timestamp
    Given a source record is being transformed
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then last_modified_date in the target should be set to the current timestamp in UTC format

  # Error Scenarios

  Scenario Outline: Error when prescriber_name_c is NULL or empty
    Given a source record with prescriber_name_c = <prescriber_name_c>
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then an error log entry should be created in pat_account_error_log with:
      | error_col      | error_message                                 |
      | prescriber_id  | "prescriber_name_c is NULL or empty"          |

    Examples:
      | prescriber_name_c |
      | NULL              |
      | ""                |

  Scenario Outline: Error when prescriber_name_c_address is NULL or empty
    Given a source record with prescriber_name_c_address = <prescriber_name_c_address>
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then an error log entry should be created in pat_account_error_log with:
      | error_col      | error_message                                 |
      | prescriber_key | "prescriber_name_c_address is NULL or empty"  |

    Examples:
      | prescriber_name_c_address |
      | NULL                     |
      | ""                       |

  Scenario Outline: Error when patinet_c is NULL or does not contain 'PAT'
    Given a source record with patinet_c = <patinet_c>
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then patient_sf_id in the target should be NULL
    And an error log entry should be created in pat_account_error_log with:
      | error_col      | error_message                                 |
      | patient_sf_id  | "patinet_c is NULL or does not contain 'PAT'" |

    Examples:
      | patinet_c |
      | NULL      |
      | "12345"   |

  Scenario Outline: Error when any of hash_key source columns are NULL
    Given a source record with patinet_c = <patinet_c>, recordtypeid = <recordtypeid>, id = <id>
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then hash_key in the target should be NULL
    And an error log entry should be created in pat_account_error_log with:
      | error_col | error_message                                      |
      | hash_key  | "One or more source columns for hash_key are NULL" |

    Examples:
      | patinet_c | recordtypeid | id     |
      | NULL      | "RT01"       | "C001" |
      | "PAT12345"| NULL         | "C001" |
      | "PAT12345"| "RT01"       | NULL   |

  Scenario: Error when last_modified_date cannot be set
    Given a system error occurs during timestamp generation
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then an error log entry should be created in pat_account_error_log with:
      | error_col          | error_message                        |
      | last_modified_date | "Failed to set last_modified_date"   |

  # Validation Rules

  Scenario Outline: Validate data types and nullability for target columns
    Given a transformed record in pat_account
    When the record is inserted
    Then the following columns must conform to data type and nullability rules:
      | Column              | Data Type | Nullability |
      | patient_foundation_shipment | string    | nullable    |
      | prescriber_id               | string    | nullable    |
      | prescriber_key              | string    | nullable    |
      | patient_sf_id               | string    | nullable    |
      | service_request_type        | string    | nullable    |
      | case_sf_id                  | string    | nullable    |
      | account_id                  | string    | nullable    |
      | hash_key                    | string    | nullable    |
      | last_modified_date          | timestamp | nullable    |

  # Data-driven scenario for all transformation rules

  Scenario Outline: Full transformation and validation for pat_account record
    Given a source record with:
      | prescriber_name_c         | prescriber_name_c_address | patinet_c   | recordtypeid | id     | accountid   |
      | <prescriber_name_c>       | <prescriber_name_c_address> | <patinet_c> | <recordtypeid> | <id> | <accountid> |
    When the transformation logic is applied
    Then the target record should have:
      | prescriber_id   | prescriber_key   | patient_sf_id   | hash_key                  | last_modified_date |
      | <prescriber_id> | <prescriber_key> | <patient_sf_id> | <hash_key>                | <last_modified_date> |

    Examples:
      | prescriber_name_c | prescriber_name_c_address | patinet_c   | recordtypeid | id     | accountid   | prescriber_id   | prescriber_key   | patient_sf_id | hash_key                | last_modified_date      |
      | "john smith"      | "michael brown"           | "PAT12345"  | "RT01"       | "C001" | "A001"      | "DR.JOHN SMITH" | "DR.MICHAEL BROWN" | "PAT12345"   | "PAT12345_RT01_C001"    | <current_timestamp>    |
      | "Dr.Jane Doe"     | "Dr.Alice White"          | "12345"     | "RT02"       | "C002" | "A002"      | "DR.JANE DOE"   | "DR.ALICE WHITE"   | NULL         | "12345_RT02_C002"       | <current_timestamp>    |
      | NULL              | "Dr.Alice White"          | "PAT67890"  | "RT03"       | "C003" | "A003"      | NULL            | "DR.ALICE WHITE"   | "PAT67890"   | "PAT67890_RT03_C003"    | <current_timestamp>    |
      | "john smith"      | NULL                      | "PAT67890"  | NULL         | "C003" | "A003"      | "DR.JOHN SMITH" | NULL               | "PAT67890"   | NULL                    | <current_timestamp>    |
      | "john smith"      | "michael brown"           | NULL        | "RT01"       | "C001" | "A001"      | "DR.JOHN SMITH" | "DR.MICHAEL BROWN" | NULL         | NULL                    | <current_timestamp>    |

